                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course is designed to offer opportunities for clinical medical students to enter the community at early stage. Through the study of related content about population&nbsp;health, the students will understand the concept of health under “Broad Perspective of Health”and health determinants of individuals, families and community groups,&nbsp; establish the concept of “Patient-Oriented Service” and “Prevention First”.&nbsp;Therefore, they will learn to apply “Life course approach to health” to promote the health of individuals, families and communities， which is helpful to implement “combined prevention and treatment services” in their future medical practice.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
